            <div xml:id="d634">

                <pb facs="0799" n="513" sameAs="frus:frus1916Supp/pg513"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72112/2897</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in Great
                        Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Laughlin</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-08-23T16:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">August 23, 1916, 4 p. m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3727. Department’s 3549, July 21, 6 p. m., and 3654, August 9, 5 p. m.,
                    Commercial Adviser British Embassy stated yesterday that he was just informed
                    that tobacco shipments for Holland, if purchased and paid for prior to August 1,
                    1916, may go forward without consignment to Netherlands Oversea Trust up to
                    August 31. This proposed arrangement if announced earlier might have gone far
                    toward covering difficulties <hi rendition="#italic">re</hi> contracts already
                    entered into pending discussion future arrangements, but in view of short
                    period—nine days—within which arrangements for shipment to seaboard, loading,
                    and dispatch vessel must be made, it is of little practicable utility.
                    Unofficially endeavor have period for shipment extended for at least three weeks
                    after August 31, so that contracts actually entered into may be taken care
                    of.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
